From b837a5d3028f372af67dea430e31a007c007708e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:52:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/46] vulkan: sparse FA kernel for GLM-5.3-Flash DSA (decode,
 verify and prefill)

The sparse path ran the coopmat1 FA shader (Br 16 heads, Bc 64) over the gathered rows. With
HSK = HSV = 512 it is slow here even without the gather (dense over 2048 rows: 54 us at one
token), and the gather adds per-step index loads and staging barriers: ~95 us per token at
any depth, so 298 us per layer for the 3-token MTP verify at 32K. More splits did not help.

flash_attn_sparse_dec.comp handles sparse FA with every head on one f16 KV head of 512 (the
MLA latent): a workgroup of 512 invocations takes 32 heads of one token over a slice of the
compacted position list. It preloads the slice, keeps its share of the scaled query heads in
registers, gathers each block of 32 rows with 16-byte loads one block ahead, and shares the
staged rows between S = QK^T and P*V (V is a view of K; a separate V is read directly).
S, softmax and O are fp32 with f16 Q and P as in the other FA paths, using v_dot2_f32_f16
where available, wave32 where the subgroup size is selectable. Splits target one round of
workgroups and go through the split_k reduce; a single split (prefill) writes dst directly.
GGML_VK_FA_SPARSE_DEC_DISABLE turns it off, GGML_VK_FA_SPARSE_DEC_MAX_N limits the batch,
GGML_VK_FA_SPARSE_DEC_WGS overrides the workgroup target.

The compaction pass issues 16 independent mask loads per lane per step instead of one, so a
row costs a few memory round trips instead of one per 64 positions.

test-backend-ops perf, Radeon 8060S, 64 heads, 2048 selected (old -> new):
  8K   n=1 107 -> 46 us, n=3 281 -> 107 us
  32K  n=1 116 -> 55 us, n=3 298 -> 119 us
  64K  n=1 125 -> 65 us, n=3 313 -> 136 us
  32K  prefill ubatch 128: 10.3 -> 4.3 ms, 512: 41.8 -> 15.3 ms
Compaction plus split reduce is ~14 us of the 32K n=1 time (25 us at 64K).

test-backend-ops: sparse cases with a separate V, 32 heads, a 1000 and a 2051 (GLM) budget,
an 8192 budget at 64K, prefill batches; GLM-shaped perf cases incl. a dense 2048 reference.

